Concrete K execution is clean: both prompt examples plus four edge composites ran through the supplied LLVM semantics and all assertions discharged, leaving `.K` with exit code 0. The remaining work is the symbolic proof; I’ve encoded the loop as a guarded circularity against a separate trial-division recurrence and am now resolving any K parser/prover issues.
diff --git a/concrete-tests.py b/concrete-tests.py
new file mode 100644
