The loop invariant itself now proves `#Top`. I found the end-to-end claim was being expanded past the loop because this `kprove` version does not use a separately selected dependency as an operational lemma in the same backend run. I’m splitting the proof into two compositional claims instead: one proves module loading/call setup reaches the exact loop invariant state, and the circular claim proves that state returns the recurrence result. Both remain ordinary, independently discharged claims—no trusted assumptions.
